wine.inf: metric-compatible fonts under the Windows file names, in every prefix's Fonts folder.

This repository's packaging change, not for WineHQ (Wine carries no third-party fonts). It follows
Proton, which links the same six names into drive_c/windows/Fonts (proton, create_fonts_symlinks;
Makefile.in's arial, arialbd, georgia, times, cour and courbd targets, proton-11.0-2e).

Some programs open a font by its file in C:\windows\Fonts (Proton's notes name FIFA 21 and 22's
arial.ttf) and fail when it is missing. The engine carries the Liberation fonts 2.1.5 (SIL Open Font
License 1.1) unchanged in share/wine/fonts, and wine.inf's BaseInstall copies them, through Wine's
own WineSourceDirs, to arial.ttf, arialbd.ttf, cour.ttf, courbd.ttf, georgia.ttf and times.ttf at
every prefix setup and update. Each line is COPYFLG_NO_OVERWRITE (patch 0016), so a font a game or
the player installed there is never replaced.

Unlike Proton, the fonts keep their own family names (Liberation Sans, Serif, Mono). Proton renames
them to Arial, Times New Roman, Georgia and Courier New because Linux has none of those. macOS ships
all four, and Wine loads them by name from the Mac (freetype.c load_mac_fonts); a renamed copy would
be a second "Arial" family competing with Apple's real one by version (font.c
insert_face_in_family_list). So names keep reaching Apple's fonts, and a program that opens the file
gets a metric-compatible one.

diff --git a/loader/wine.inf.in b/loader/wine.inf.in
index 942a2cf..f35b5e4 100644
--- a/loader/wine.inf.in
+++ b/loader/wine.inf.in
@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@ AddService=MountMgr,0x800,MountMgrService
 RegisterDlls=RegisterDllsSection
 WineFakeDlls=FakeDlls
 UpdateInis=SystemIni
-CopyFiles=ColorFiles,EtcFiles,InfFiles,NlsFiles,SortFiles,WinmdFiles
+CopyFiles=ColorFiles,EtcFiles,FontFiles,InfFiles,NlsFiles,SortFiles,WinmdFiles
 AddReg=\
     Classes,\
     ContentIndex,\
@@ -1220,6 +1220,16 @@ networks,"@%11%\ws2_32.dll,-2"
 protocol,"@%11%\ws2_32.dll,-3"
 services,"@%11%\ws2_32.dll,-4"
 
+[FontFiles]
+; Metric-compatible fonts under the file names some programs open in the
+; Fonts folder (the set Proton links); an existing file is never replaced.
+arial.ttf,LiberationSans-Regular.ttf,,0x10
+arialbd.ttf,LiberationSans-Bold.ttf,,0x10
+cour.ttf,LiberationMono-Regular.ttf,,0x10
+courbd.ttf,LiberationMono-Bold.ttf,,0x10
+georgia.ttf,LiberationSerif-Regular.ttf,,0x10
+times.ttf,LiberationSerif-Regular.ttf,,0x10
+
 [InfFiles]
 input.inf,"@%12%\hidclass.sys,-1"
 mouhid.inf,"@%12%\mouhid.sys,-1"
@@ -1322,6 +1332,7 @@ windows.ui.winmd
 windows.ui.xaml.winmd
 
 [WineSourceDirs]
+FontFiles = fonts
 NlsFiles  = nls
 SortFiles = nls
 WinmdFiles = winmd,include
@@ -1329,6 +1340,7 @@ WinmdFiles = winmd,include
 [DestinationDirs]
 ColorFiles = 23
 EtcFiles  = 12,etc
+FontFiles = 20
 InfFiles  = 17
 NlsFiles  = 11
 SortFiles = 10,globalization\sorting
